---
import catalog from '../../../assets/materials/catalog.json';
import {asset} from '../data/catalog';
import {url} from '../lib/urls';
interface Props {path:string}
const {path}=Astro.props;
const materials=catalog.entries;
const renderers=[{id:'mesh',label:'Forward PBR'},{id:'sdf',label:'SDF ray marching'},{id:'rt',label:'Hardware RT'}];
const variants=renderers.flatMap(renderer=>['dusk','dawn'].map(phase=>({renderer:renderer.id,label:renderer.label,phase,id:`materials-${renderer.id}-${phase}`})));
const poster=asset('materials-mesh-dusk');const film=asset('materials-mesh-dusk-film');
---
<section class="section material-library" id="material-library" data-material-library>
  <span id="mesh-materials" class="anchor-target"></span>
  <div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">The complete library</span><h2>One library. Three renderers.</h2></div></div>
  <div class="library-controls" data-library-controls hidden><div class="renderer-controls" role="group" aria-label="Material renderer">
    <button class="filter" data-renderer="mesh" aria-pressed="true">Forward PBR</button>
    <button class="filter" data-renderer="sdf" aria-pressed="false">SDF ray marching</button>
    <button class="filter" data-renderer="rt" aria-pressed="false">Hardware RT</button>
  </div><div class="renderer-controls" role="group" aria-label="Lighting transition">
    <button class="filter" data-phase="dusk" aria-pressed="true">Dusk</button>
    <button class="filter" data-phase="dawn" aria-pressed="false">Dawn</button>
  </div></div>
  <figure class="scene-media library-stage"><div class="movie"><video data-library-film controls playsinline preload="none" poster={url(poster.file,path)} width={film.width} height={film.height} aria-label="Twelve material spheres · Forward PBR · dusk"><source src={url(film.file,path)} type="video/mp4"/><p><a data-library-download href={url(film.file,path)}>Download the film</a>.</p></video></div><figcaption class="media-foot" data-renderer-caption aria-live="polite">Forward PBR · dusk · native recorded playback</figcaption></figure>
  {variants.map(v=><a hidden data-material-variant data-renderer-key={v.renderer} data-phase-key={v.phase} href={url(asset(`${v.id}-film`).file,path)} data-poster={url(asset(v.id).file,path)}>{v.renderer} · {v.phase}</a>)}
  <p class="note">Twelve shared recipes, the same sphere layout, camera and clear-sky lighting timeline. Switch renderers to compare the same moment. These films show environment reflection and refraction; neighboring spheres do not appear in either.</p>
  <a class="source-link" href="https://github.com/byebyebryan/cubey/blob/main/docs/notes/raytracing-material-workshop-guide.md">Run the matched scenes ↗</a>
  <noscript><p class="note">Other films: {variants.slice(1).map(v=><a href={url(asset(`${v.id}-film`).file,path)}>{v.label} · {v.phase} · </a>)}</p></noscript>
  <div class="material-glass-study"><h3>Three ways through glass.</h3><p class="note">The same tinted glass under frozen lighting. Forward PBR estimates an exit ray; SDF follows implicit boundaries; hardware RT follows triangulated boundaries. Their surface detail and optical approximations can still differ.</p>
    <div class="material-glass-comparison">{renderers.map(renderer=>{const image=asset(`materials-${renderer.id}-glass`);return <figure><img src={url(image.file,path)} width={image.width} height={image.height} alt={`Tinted glass · ${renderer.label} · shared clear atmosphere`} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{renderer.label}</figcaption></figure>;})}</div>
  </div>
  <details class="material-inspection"><summary>Inspect individual materials</summary><p class="note">Separate stills under frozen lighting. The order below matches the rows in the film.</p>
  <div class="material-grid">{materials.map(m=>{const mesh=asset(`materials-mesh-${m.id}`);const sdf=asset(`materials-sdf-${m.id}`);const rt=asset(`materials-rt-${m.id}`);return <figure class="material-tile" data-material={m.id}>
    <a data-material-link href={url(mesh.file,path)} data-mesh={url(mesh.file,path)} data-sdf={url(sdf.file,path)} data-rt={url(rt.file,path)} aria-label={`Open ${m.label} · Forward PBR`}><img data-material-image src={url(mesh.file,path)} data-mesh={url(mesh.file,path)} data-sdf={url(sdf.file,path)} data-rt={url(rt.file,path)} data-label={m.label} width={mesh.width} height={mesh.height} alt={`${m.label} · Forward PBR mesh specimen`} loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></a>
    <figcaption><h3>{m.label}</h3><p>{m.description}</p></figcaption>
  </figure>;})}</div>
  <noscript>{renderers.slice(1).map(renderer=><p class="note">{renderer.label} stills: {materials.map(m=><a href={url(asset(`materials-${renderer.id}-${m.id}`).file,path)}>{m.label} · </a>)}</p>)}</noscript></details>
  <details><summary>How the renderers share materials</summary><p class="note">All three use the same recipe library and shared atmosphere lighting. Forward PBR shades mesh spheres; SDF ray marching shades implicit solids; hardware RT intersects triangulated spheres. Forward and SDF rough glass filter environment radiance, while RT samples bounded rough dielectric paths. Local specimen shadows and diffuse GI are disabled in this comparison. This is a matched lighting study, with distinct optical approximations.</p><a class="source-link" href="https://github.com/byebyebryan/cubey/blob/main/docs/architecture/material-recipes.md">Shared recipes and renderer details ↗</a></details>
</section>

<style>
  .material-glass-study{margin:32px 0}
  .material-glass-comparison{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px}
  .material-glass-comparison img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:8px}
  .material-glass-comparison figcaption{margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted);font-size:14px}
  .material-inspection .material-tile img{aspect-ratio:16/9}
  @media(max-width:620px){.material-glass-comparison{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
